From 8dc0da607c53631d17de1b10d82e9e0f1d6d29c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:44:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 017/206] refactor(shorebird): review cleanups to wrapper
 Layout

Four fixes from Task 1 code review:

- wrapper.cc referenced "Task 4" for the empty-range rejection test; that
  test lives in Task 3.
- Dropped a premature include of vm/growable_array.h from wrapper.h. Nothing
  in the header uses it yet -- MallocGrowableArray arrives with
  WrapperAllocator. Build is clean without it.
- Copyright line 1 now uses two spaces after "authors." to match the project
  convention (see shorebird/link_info.h).
- Renamed WrapperLayout_CountIsDerivedNotHardcoded to
  WrapperLayout_CountIsConsistentWithPageFields. The old name overclaimed: the
  test reads all four fields off the Layout that fromTemplate() already
  populated, so a config hardcoding kNumWrappersPerPage = 2014 would still
  pass it. It guards internal consistency, not derivation. What actually pins
  the values is DerivedCountsMatchTheirDwarf, which ties inputs and output to
  their DWARF literals. Comment now says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

